Required corrections

1. Use the authoritative backend token-issuance operation.
2. Validate the authenticated user and applicable call permissions before issuing tokens.
3. Apply the minimum required Twilio Voice SDK grants and token lifetime.
4. Preserve secure token refresh and expired-token handling.
5. Prevent unauthorised clients from initiating or joining calls.
6. Prevent duplicate call initiation caused by repeated UI events or network retries.
7. Keep frontend call state synchronised with authoritative backend state.
8. Handle disconnects, reconnects, rejected calls, and network interruptions.
9. Ensure call termination updates both the client and authoritative call record.
10. Preserve existing device-selection and microphone-permission handling where supported.
11. Ensure media resources and SDK listeners are cleaned up correctly.
12. Avoid unnecessary duplicate SDK instances or competing call-state managers.

