14. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The implementation is complete only when the following conditions are satisfied.

A. One authoritative call-control architecture

Call initiation, token issuance, call control, and authoritative state updates have one verified backend authority.

B. Correct Twilio/WebRTC relationship

The existing supported Voice SDK and WebRTC media architecture remain functional, with privileged operations controlled by the backend.

C. Unified call records

Twilio call identifiers, Rentmaikar call IDs, participants, status updates, and recordings are consistently correlated in Supabase.

D. Reliable callbacks

Twilio callbacks are validated, idempotent, and safe against duplicate or out-of-order delivery.

E. Secure recording access

Recording metadata and media are protected by the applicable authorisation, RLS, and storage controls.

F. Voice morphing is preserved

Existing morphing functionality is integrated into the actual supported processing path.

G. No false claims about morphing

Real-time voice morphing is marked complete only when transformed audio is verified in the live media path. Post-call processing is not misrepresented as real-time transformation.

H. No duplicate call-control authorities

Legacy functions no longer independently execute conflicting privileged operations.

I. No unrelated regressions

Authentication, payments, messaging, booking, and other unrelated workflows remain intact.

J. Evidence-based completion

Every claimed result is supported by source inspection, tests, or verified deployment/runtime evidence.

